-- title:
--   Constant reduction of a unit along an interior circle
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, and $F$ a field extension of $L$. Let `An` be an annulus of $F$ over $A$: a set `An.dom` of places of $F/L$ (each place being a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $L$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring), a parameter `An.param` $\in F$ and a modulus `An.modulus` in the maximal ideal of $A$, subject to the annulus axioms — every $P \in$ `An.dom` has residue field generated by $L$ (so that $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$, evaluation at $P$ through the induced section, takes values in $L$), `An.param` is $P$-integral with value in the maximal ideal of $A$, nonzero, and dividing `An.modulus` there; the places of the domain are parametrised bijectively by the admissible values of the parameter; $P.\mathrm{ord}(\mathrm{param} - P(\mathrm{param})) = 1$; and the unit principle for functions without zeros or poles on the domain. Assume: every nonzero $f \in F$ has only finitely many places of `An.dom` at which $\mathrm{ord}\, f \neq 0$; an element $c \in L$ with $v(\mathrm{modulus}) < v(c) < 1$ for the valuation $v$ of $A$; the residue field of $A$ is infinite; there exist $b, b' \in L$ with $v(c) < v(b) < 1$ and $v(\mathrm{modulus}) < v(b') < v(c)$; and $u \in F$ is integral at every place of `An.dom` with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,u$ lying in $A$ and a unit there, for all $P \in$ `An.dom`. Then for any two places $P, Q \in$ `An.dom` with $v(P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param}) = v(c) = v(Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,\mathrm{param})$, the residues in the residue field of $A$ of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,u$ and $Q.\mathrm{evalAt}\,u$ coincide.
--
--   This is the maximum principle for an annulus in the form needed here: a function with unit values at all places of the annulus has constant reduction along each interior circle, the annulus axioms themselves pinning only the absolute values of unit parts and not their residues. It is used to construct the reduction homomorphism to a rational function field attached to an interior circle and to establish the slope laws of that chart, in [`AlgebraicCurve.Annulus.exists_ringHom_ratFunc_of_valuation_lt_of_exists_lt`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Annulus.exists_ringHom_ratFunc_of_valuation_lt_of_exists_lt) and [`AlgebraicCurve.Annulus.mapDomain_and_slope_of_valuation_lt_of_exists_lt`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Annulus.mapDomain_and_slope_of_valuation_lt_of_exists_lt).
